#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "61c51284-18f0-5398-857b-7687228e8df8" :question/math-academy-id "e-7985" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x^2}{9}, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192618 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "c755eddf-3b0d-5a33-aa13-e6a3f7da4244" :question/math-academy-id "e-7986" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[7X-4].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{3x^2}{7}, \\quad 1 <        x <        2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[7X-4] = 7 \\textrm E[X] - 4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{28}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[7X-4] & =7\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{45}{28}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b84b8fb-5ad7-5c4f-af44-b6d1dc9310c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable With a Piecewise PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "3a11b9e3-60c8-57f3-8ec6-4ff378d0db62" :question/math-academy-id "e-7987" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n![](images/98/98b997e3016e9ca5538863c3faa19ac017f90e8bcdeba40e09c03aba28c4ace4.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{3x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{31}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e870738-b0c3-5a45-a958-0a8ab816e8ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190325} {:answer/id #uuid "a6105e5f-10e9-560d-b7e2-58cef8643cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190326} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b9be8a-5521-5f98-8ff2-7e30822d0744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190327} {:answer/id #uuid "fa218f47-8a14-524f-b582-ac051f2f4b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190328} {:answer/id #uuid "6095d4ff-1396-56a8-a23b-76ac5552bb6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190329}] :answer-field/id #uuid "dbb35035-e4ad-5dfe-8305-ac38b8d7b733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186190324}] :question/id #uuid "b377af59-2f66-52f6-af8e-4fb410b37e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-149715" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $E[5X - 2]$.\n\n$f(x) = {1 - x^{3},\\begin{vmatrix}0 < x \\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{8},\\end{vmatrix}1 \\le x < 3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c9587e-71e5-566c-a7c0-2ca7d8543d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424058} {:answer/id #uuid "44d46d21-8790-5b62-b822-b15cfffb758c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424060} {:answer/id #uuid "6ddc91ad-5eb5-580c-aec8-05f1a65ef396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424063} {:answer/id #uuid "77b11337-68cc-5792-80b0-2420a4a46582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424065} {:answer/id #uuid "f27e69cb-8e5b-5f27-b7bd-fd886daab64b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b11337-68cc-5792-80b0-2420a4a46582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424065} :answer-field/id #uuid "174c2ec8-e1f1-51fa-bb13-18381c6477ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3754a443-839d-5055-afd8-172b5271b8be" :question/math-academy-id "q-90386" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{36}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493212b2-48a2-5243-a9c9-38c8ad4f746e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424061} {:answer/id #uuid "58440bd6-5f91-58ba-8252-d7a100bf2bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424062} {:answer/id #uuid "73b5e0f3-2a9f-5fb2-98c7-0b0e8e8b99a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424064} {:answer/id #uuid "955a942b-f31a-5981-97c6-1e16d11283d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424070} {:answer/id #uuid "fd63a7fa-8fda-54c4-8de2-4fa95151be2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "493212b2-48a2-5243-a9c9-38c8ad4f746e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424061} :answer-field/id #uuid "807b5737-467e-51a3-be92-0cedb472eebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6256bcf-ce6c-599c-ab9b-d80ffcce67e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-90455" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[8X-3].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9},\\,0<x<3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[8X-3]=8\\text{E}[X]-3\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[8X-3] & =8\\text{E}[X]-3 \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{9}{4}-3 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
